# Local dev services (UAT keep / post-merge stop)

**测时期间可复测；合进 main 后停掉本线程端口。人停了就别再起。**

## During the task (before land)

While implementing / UAT / before merge:

1. Prefer **reuse** an already-healthy web that serves **this** checkout + branch over starting extras.
2. Leave **local Supabase** running when this thread used `npm run dev` + supabase-local.
3. Report the live base when testing (`http://localhost:<port>`, `MESA_UAT_BASE` if not `:3000`).
4. Do **not** start a new web solely because a checklist step finished and nothing is listening.

## After merge / land (hard — no extra ask)

When the user asked to **merge / 合进 main / land** and the land done-gate in [`git-local-merge-push.mdc`](./git-local-merge-push.mdc) has passed:

1. **Stop listen ports this thread started** for the task — web (`next dev` / `npm run dev|cloud|stage`), ops (`npm run dev:ops`), and any extra UAT Next (`3002+` / `.next-uat` / etc.).
2. Confirm PID/cwd/port belong to **this** conversation (terminal metadata / PID you spawned) before `kill`.
3. Leave **local Supabase / Docker DB** up (do not `db reset` / `compose down -v` for cleanup).
4. Do **not** kill ports / agents started by **other** sessions or by Will outside this thread.
5. Closing note: which ports were stopped; do not leave feature-UAT Next running “方便复测” after land.

Skip port stop only if Will explicitly says keep the server（例如「合完别停 web」）.

## Human stop / aborted shell (hard)

If Will stops a listen port, kills a terminal, or a system notification says a **this-thread** `next dev` / `npm run dev|cloud|stage` / ops shell was **aborted** / **terminated_by_user**:

1. **Do not restart it.** Brief note only (“已停”).
2. Aborted-task “follow-up” does **not** authorize relaunching web/dev/ops/print-agent.
3. Restart only when Will **explicitly** asks in-thread（例如「再起 web」「起 :3005」）.

## Session hygiene (allowed anytime)

Stop processes that are **clearly started by this thread** and no longer needed — e.g. a second Next after switching to another base, or a finished one-shot build/lint shell. Same PID/cwd ownership check.

## Forbidden

- Killing or reclaiming a listen port / agent / `npm run dev|cloud|stage` / ops / print-agent you did **not** start in this thread (includes other Cursor chats and human terminals) — same spirit as [`dev-port-isolation.mdc`](./dev-port-isolation.mdc)
- **Auto-restarting** a web/dev/ops process after Will stopped it or after an aborted-shell notification
- `supabase db reset`, `docker compose down -v`, deleting local DB volumes, or any hard local DB wipe — unless the user explicitly asks in-thread
- Stopping local Supabase / Docker DB “for cleanup” after UAT or merge
- Leaving **this thread’s** feature/UAT web listening after a completed merge/land
- Broad `pkill -f next` / `killall node` / port-wide kills that can hit other sessions

## Order of operations

**End of implement/UAT (no merge yet):** keep this-thread usable web (+ Supabase if used); report base; optional stop of true extras only.

**After merge/land done-gate:** stop this-thread web/ops listen ports → report stopped ports → do not touch other sessions or the DB → do not start a replacement web unless Will asks.
